THEO: Then it’s hiding. (A long pause. A car passes in the distance.)
MARA: I’m not saying you’re wrong. I’m saying the sun is going down.', 'HUM-BANK-N1-P06'),
  ('HUM-BANK-N1-P06-Q4', 'humanities', 'hard', 60, 'Which line shows Mara softening her approach?', '["“I’m not saying you’re wrong.”","“We could just ask someone.”","“That was an hour ago.”","“Roads don’t move, Theo.”"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Mara reassures Theo before raising her real worry, which is a gentler way to disagree.', 'MARA: (not looking up from the map) We could just ask someone.
